{"isprs_int_j_geo_inf__volume__10": "The predicate \"volume\" refers to a specific edition or issue number of a journal, indicating its sequence within a given year or publication period. It is used to organize, identify, and locate individual issues or contributions within the journal. This helps in understanding the placement and sequence of articles published in a particular year or installment.|Here is another description: The predicate \"volume\" indicates the specific edition or issue number of the journal in which a particular article or set of articles is published, helping to organize and identify content within the journal's publication timeline.|Here is another description: The predicate \"volume\" refers to the specific edition or issue number of a journal within a given year. It helps to organize and identify the placement of articles within the journal's publication sequence."},
