{"unimodal_data": "Unimodal data refers to data that consists of a single mode or type, such as text, images, or video, as opposed to multimodal data which combines multiple types.|Here is another description: Unimodal data refers to the use of a single type of data for analysis, which in the context of disaster data classification, can be either text-based or image-based methods. This approach focuses on extracting useful information from one data source to understand and respond to disaster situations.|Here is another description: Unimodal data refers to the use of a single type of data for analysis in disaster data classification methods. This approach focuses on either text or image data exclusively to extract relevant information and insights following a disaster event."},
