{"two_features__were_fused__by_means_of_a_concatenating_operation": "The predicate \"were fused\" indicates the action of combining or merging the two features. This fusion is a critical step in preparing the data for the classification process, enhancing the model's ability to make accurate predictions."},
{"by_means_of_a_concatenating_operation": "The object \"by means of a concatenating operation\" describes the specific method used to fuse the two features. Concatenation involves joining the features end-to-end, creating a single, unified feature set that can be processed by the classification model."},
{"final_classification": "The final classification refers to the conclusive step in a machine learning or data processing pipeline where the data is categorized into predefined classes based on the features extracted and processed through the model."},
{"final_classification__was_accomplished__by_three_fully_connected_layers_and_one_softmax_layer": "The predicate \"was accomplished\" indicates the successful completion of the final classification process, suggesting that the intended categorization of data was effectively carried out using the specified model architecture."},
{"by_three_fully_connected_layers_and_one_softmax_layer": "The object \"by three fully connected layers and one SoftMax layer\" describes the architecture used to achieve the final classification. This setup typically involves neural network layers where the fully connected layers process the input features, and the SoftMax layer outputs a probability distribution over the possible classes for the final decision."},
