{"images__need_to_be__cropped_and_resized": "The phrase \"need to be\" indicates a requirement or necessity for the images to undergo a specific transformation. In this context, it signifies that the images must be altered in a certain way to meet the prerequisites for training a neural network."},
{"cropped_and_resized": "The object \"cropped and resized\" describes the specific transformations that the images must undergo. Cropping involves trimming the images to remove unwanted or extraneous parts, while resizing adjusts the dimensions of the images to a uniform size, in this case, 224x224 pixels."},
{"images__resized_to__224_224": "The predicate \"resized to\" indicates a preprocessing step where the dimensions of the images are altered to meet specific requirements for model training. This resizing is crucial for ensuring uniformity across the dataset, which is essential for the consistent application of the model."},
