{"methodology": "The methodology refers to the systematic, theoretical analysis of the methods applied to a field of study, comprising the theoretical analysis of the body of methods and principles associated with a branch of knowledge. In this context, it involves the specific techniques and procedures used by Zhiqiang Zou and his colleagues to conduct their research.|Here is another description: The methodology refers to the systematic, theoretical analysis of the methods applied to a field of study. In this context, it encompasses the strategies, procedures, and techniques employed by the authors to conduct their research, ensuring the validity and reliability of their findings."},
