{"text_messages_exclusively": "Text messages exclusively refer to the sole use of textual data, without incorporating other forms of media such as images or videos, for the purpose of analysis. In the context of veracity analysis, this means that only the written content of messages is considered for evaluating the truth of the information conveyed.|Here is another description: Text messages exclusively refer to the use of only textual data, without incorporating other forms of data such as images or audio, for the purpose of conducting sentiment analysis.|Here is another description: Text messages exclusively refers to the sole use of textual data from messages for the purpose of detection. In the context of cyberbullying, this means that the analysis is conducted purely on the text content of messages, without incorporating other forms of data such as images or audio."},
