{"limited_multimodal_fusion_methods": "Limited multimodal fusion methods refer to techniques that combine information from multiple data modalities, such as images and text, but are constrained in their approach or application. These methods aim to enhance the performance of machine learning models by leveraging the complementary nature of different data types."},
{"limited_multimodal_fusion_methods__integrate__images_and_text_information_and_are_applied_to_classification_tasks": "The predicate \"integrate\" in this context signifies the process of combining and synthesizing information from different modalities, such as images and text, to create a unified representation. This integration is crucial for multimodal machine learning tasks, as it allows models to leverage the strengths of each data type to improve overall performance."},
{"images_and_text_information_and_are_applied_to_classification_tasks": "Images and text information, when integrated, provide a richer dataset for classification tasks. This combination allows machine learning models to capture both visual and textual nuances, leading to more accurate and robust classifications. Classification tasks involve categorizing data into predefined classes based on the features extracted from the integrated modalities."},
