{"a_multimodal_fusion_method_to_classify_disaster_images": "A multimodal fusion method to classify disaster images is a technique that combines information from multiple data sources, such as images and text, to improve the accuracy of image classification. This method involves extracting features from both images and text and then fusing them to make a final classification decision."},
{"image_feature_extractor": "The image feature extractor is a component within a multimodal fusion method designed to classify disaster images. It is responsible for processing visual data.|Here is another description: The image feature extractor is one of the three modules in the multimodal classification model, responsible for extracting features from image data to be used in the classification process.|Here is another description: The image feature extractor is a module designed to extract features from images, which is crucial for various image processing tasks. It is part of a larger system that utilizes convolutional neural networks (CNNs) to analyze and interpret visual data."},
