{"a_visual_sentiment_model_to_analyze_disaster_related_images": "A visual sentiment model to analyze disaster-related images is a computational model designed to interpret and classify the emotional content or sentiment expressed in images related to disasters. This model aims to extract emotional cues from visual data, which can be crucial for understanding public reaction and needs during disaster events."},
{"multimodal_data__used_for__sa_establishment_and_information_extraction": "The predicate \"used for\" indicates the purpose or application of multimodal data in the context of disaster management. It highlights how multimodal data is employed to achieve specific goals, such as establishing situational awareness and extracting relevant information."},
{"sa_establishment_and_information_extraction": "SA establishment and information extraction are critical components in disaster management. Situational Awareness (SA) involves understanding the current state of a disaster, while information extraction pertains to the process of gathering and analyzing data to derive actionable insights. Together, they enable effective decision-making and response strategies during disasters."},
{"dao_et_al": "Dao et al. refers to a group of researchers who have contributed to the field of disaster data classification, specifically through the development of multimodal data fusion methods. Their work is part of a broader effort to enhance situational awareness during disasters by leveraging various types of data from social media."},
