{"a_multimodal_twitter_dataset_with_spatiotemporal_features": "A multimodal Twitter dataset with spatiotemporal features refers to a collection of tweets that include various types of data (text, images) and are annotated with information about time and location. This dataset is designed to support research on the impact and responses to natural disasters as captured on Twitter."},
{"crisismmd__consists_of__several_thousands_of_manually_annotated_tweets": "The phrase \"consists of\" indicates that CrisisMMD is composed of or includes a specific set of elements, in this case, tweets that have been manually annotated."},
{"several_thousands_of_manually_annotated_tweets": "Several thousands of manually annotated tweets form the core content of the CrisisMMD dataset. These tweets were collected during significant natural disaster events and have been meticulously labeled to provide valuable insights into the nature and impact of these disasters."},
{"tweets": "The subject, \"tweets,\" refers to the individual messages posted on the social media platform Twitter. In the context of the dataset, these tweets are part of a collection that has been manually annotated for specific characteristics related to natural disasters."},
{"tweets__were_collected_during__seven_major_natural_disaster_events": "The predicate, \"were collected during,\" indicates the temporal and situational context in which the tweets were gathered. It signifies that the tweets were captured and compiled as they occurred in real-time during the specified natural disaster events."},
{"seven_major_natural_disaster_events": "The object, \"seven major natural disaster events,\" encompasses a series of significant catastrophic occurrences that had a profound impact on affected regions. These events include Hurricane Irma 2017, Hurricane Harvey 2017, Hurricane Maria 2017, the California Wildfires 2017, the Mexico Earthquake 2017, the Iraq\u2013Iran Border Earthquake 2017, and the Sri Lanka Floods 2017.|Here is another description: The seven major natural disaster events represent the distinct categories into which the datasets are divided. These categories likely include events such as earthquakes, floods, hurricanes, and other significant natural occurrences that are critical for the study's analysis and model training."},
{"hurricane_irma": "Hurricane Irma was a powerful and destructive tropical cyclone that occurred in the Atlantic Ocean during the 2017 hurricane season. It was one of the most intense Atlantic hurricanes on record, causing widespread damage and significant loss of life across several Caribbean islands and the southeastern United States.|Here is another description: Hurricane Irma is a powerful and destructive tropical cyclone that caused widespread damage and loss of life in the Caribbean and the United States in September 2017.|Here is another description: Hurricane Irma is a powerful and destructive tropical cyclone that caused widespread damage and significant impact across multiple regions.|Here is another description: Hurricane Irma is a powerful and destructive tropical cyclone that caused widespread damage and loss of life in the Caribbean and the United States in 2017."},
{"hurricane_irma__occurred_in__2017": "The predicate \"occurred in\" signifies the temporal context in which Hurricane Irma took place, linking the hurricane to a specific year."},
