{"hurricane_harvey": "Hurricane Harvey, a powerful and destructive tropical cyclone, struck the Gulf Coast of the United States in August 2017, particularly impacting Texas. It caused widespread flooding, significant damage to infrastructure and homes, and was part of the CrisisMMD dataset for analysis and annotation.|Here is another description: Hurricane Harvey was a powerful and destructive storm that caused widespread damage and flooding in various parts of Texas, including Bayside.|Here is another description: Hurricane Harvey was a powerful and destructive tropical cyclone that made landfall in Texas in August 2017, causing widespread damage and flooding.|Here is another description: Hurricane Harvey is a powerful and devastating tropical cyclone that struck the Texas coast, leading to significant flooding, wind damage, and overall destruction in the affected areas."},
{"hurricane_harvey__occurred_in__2017": "The predicate \"occurred in\" specifies the temporal context in which Hurricane Harvey took place. It indicates the year during which the hurricane happened, providing a timeframe for the disaster event."},
{"hurricane_maria": "Hurricane Maria, a powerful and destructive tropical cyclone, struck several Caribbean islands, including Puerto Rico, in September 2017. It caused widespread devastation, significant damage, and loss of life, necessitating substantial recovery efforts.|Here is another description: Hurricane Maria is a powerful and destructive tropical cyclone that caused significant damage and loss of life in the Caribbean, particularly in Puerto Rico, during its passage in September 2017.|Here is another description: Hurricane Maria is a powerful and destructive tropical cyclone that caused significant damage and loss of life in the Caribbean, particularly in Puerto Rico and the U.S. Virgin Islands.|Here is another description: Hurricane Maria is a powerful and destructive tropical cyclone that caused significant damage and loss of life in the Caribbean, particularly in Puerto Rico and the U.S. Virgin Islands."},
