{"labels__are_based_on__three_different_classification_tasks": "The phrase \"are based on\" indicates that the labels are derived from or depend upon the outcomes of specific classification tasks designed to evaluate the content of tweets and images."},
{"three_different_classification_tasks": "The three different classification tasks involve evaluating the relevance of tweets and images to disasters, categorizing informative content into specific disaster-related topics, and assessing the severity of damage depicted in images related to infrastructure and utility damage."},
{"task_1": "Task 1 is a multifaceted experimental task within various studies and datasets, primarily focused on evaluating the effectiveness and relevance of data modalities\u2014such as tweets, images, and their combinations\u2014in the context of natural disasters or humanitarian aid efforts. It involves classification tasks to categorize data as \"Informative\" or \"Not informative,\" assessing the performance of image feature extractor models, and comparing unimodal methods with multimodal approaches to benchmark their effectiveness.|Here is another description: Task 1 is the initial step in a series of tasks aimed at managing and assessing disaster situations using multimodal machine learning methods. Its primary goal is to gather and process information relevant to disasters."},
{"task_1__evaluates__whether_the_data_is_related_to_the_disaster_or_humanitarian_aid": "The predicate \"evaluates\" in Task 1 refers to the process of assessing and categorizing tweets and images based on their relevance to the disaster or humanitarian aid. This evaluation determines whether the content is informative about the disaster or not."},
{"whether_the_data_is_related_to_the_disaster_or_humanitarian_aid": "The object \"whether the data is related to the disaster or humanitarian aid\" refers to the criterion used in Task 1 to classify tweets and images. It involves determining if the content provides information relevant to the disaster, such as updates, aid efforts, or impacts, or if it is unrelated to the event."},
{"task_2": "Task 2 is an experimental task focused on classifying tweets and images related to natural disasters into specific subcategories using the CrisisMMD dataset. It involves a two-step process: filtering out irrelevant instances and categorizing the remaining data. The task evaluates the effectiveness of text and image modalities, using both unimodal and multimodal methods, to achieve accurate classifications. It includes training a multimodal model, setting the number of epochs, and assessing model accuracy. Task 2 follows the extraction of disaster-related information (Task 1) and precedes the assessment of damage severity (Task 3)."},
