{"multimodal_classification_model": "The multimodal classification model is a sophisticated framework designed to process and analyze data from multiple modalities, such as images and text, to perform classification tasks."},
{"multimodal_classification_model__consists_of__three_modules": "The phrase \"consists of\" indicates that the multimodal classification model is made up of or includes several distinct components that work together to achieve its functionality."},
{"three_modules": "The three modules that make up the multimodal classification model are specialized components: an image feature extractor that processes visual data, a textual feature extractor that handles textual information, and a multimodal fusion module that integrates the extracted features from both modalities to make informed classifications.|Here is another description: The three modules refer to the components of the multimodal classification model, which are designed to process and integrate different types of data for analysis.|Here is another description: The three modules refer to the components of the multimodal classification model framework, which are designed to handle different types of data inputs and processes.|Here is another description: The three modules refer to the components of the multimodal classification model, which are designed to handle different types of data inputs."},
