{"model__pretrained_on__imagenet": "The phrase \"pretrained on\" indicates that the model has undergone an initial training phase using a specific dataset to learn general features before being fine-tuned for a particular application."},
{"imagenet": "ImageNet is a large-scale dataset consisting of millions of images categorized into thousands of classes, used for training and evaluating machine learning models in computer vision tasks."},
{"pretraining": "Pretraining refers to the initial training phase of a machine learning model, where it learns general features from a large dataset before being fine-tuned for a specific task. In this context, pretraining is done using the ImageNet dataset."},
